 "robot_upload_note": "D154 (4) / D150 SYNC (1): robot history frames upload PER FRAME AS CAPTURED, for ALL arms, replacing D68's fixed 30-s batches. One `history_batch` record per D2 frame, offered at t0 + the frame's session-local capture time, carrying exactly one frame_ref and one frame's bytes. The record KIND, its fields and the D2 token accounting are unchanged, so the emulator, the coordinator, `cstate` and every arm need no change; `cum_tokens` still carries the session's running total and the 31-token D2 header is still charged once per session, on its first holding (the D101 preload where there is one, otherwise the first frame). ONE INTENDED DIFFERENCE BEYOND PACKAGING, named because it is visible in the counts: under batch-30s a window whose END falls after the run horizon is dropped whole, taking frames captured BEFORE the horizon with it; per-frame keeps every frame captured before the horizon, which is the point of the contract. Earlier cells are labelled upload-30s.",
